{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghu7Yur8ZRpdkaC63sSe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I could not solve this exactly. I did not have the full Tanabe–Sugano d⁵ quartet secular matrices to hand, so the Dq value below is an estimate and not a rigorous fit.\n\n**What is exact.** The ⁴A₁(G) and ⁴E(G) states have the same energy, 10B + 5C, and this does not depend on Dq. Setting this equal to the ⁴E band at 23 000 cm⁻¹ gives 10B + 5C = 23 000 cm⁻¹.\n\n**What I estimated.** Dq and B must be fitted to the ⁴T₁(G) and ⁴T₂(G) bands (19 240 and 21 890 cm⁻¹). Both states fall with increasing Dq and are mixed with ⁴T₁(P) and ⁴T₂(D). I compared the band spacings with those of a similar Mn²⁺ complex whose parameters I remember approximately. That comparison puts Dq/B at about 0.7–0.8, which gives Dq ≈ 500 cm⁻¹. That is a weak field, which is plausible for a bromide.\n\n**Resulting values.**\n- B ≈ 650 cm⁻¹ (taken as a representative Mn²⁺ value, not fitted).\n- C = (23 000 − 10B)/5 ≈ 3 300 cm⁻¹, so C/B ≈ 5.1, which is reasonable for Mn²⁺.\n\nThese are approximate: roughly Dq ≈ 500, B ≈ 650 and C ≈ 3 300 cm⁻¹. To fit all three parameters properly, diagonalize the ⁴T₁ and ⁴T₂ matrices numerically.\n\n{\"Dq\": 500, \"B\": 650, \"C\": 3300, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"C follows exactly from 10B+5C = 23000 cm^-1 (the 4E band), but Dq and B are estimated by comparison with another Mn(II) complex, not fitted with the full Tanabe-Sugano matrices.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6b0538d-2